A couple of nights ago I sat down at nethack once more.

Sure, why not a gnomish healer.  Even try the protection racket.

A generous shopkeeper, a not very useful bonesfile, and a loyal pet got
me nine points without much problem.

Sokoban provided a necklase, and then I wandered down to the bottom of
the mines for my rock.  Mm, a nice bones file, but the bag is cursed.

The dungeon is full of altars, so I picked up the vorpulblade--a bit
sharper than the scalpel.  Down I continued, with pets coming and going.

The rings of free action & levitation made medusa quite easy, and she
was followed by three levels of mazes. After duking it out, and comeing
a bit too close, with the first two minotaus, I used some fire on the
third one.

Then a regular level, which had a room with an altar and a sink.  Hmm.
However, I woke up the black pudding in the throne room (the third so
far, in addition to a  huge leprechaun halls and a huge behive).  I dug
a tunnel behind the altar, and along came the puddings.  After a few, it
occured to me that it would be worthwhile to relearn a healing spell or
two, so I could make them breed faster.  Still poking them with a dull
dagger and checking with my stethoscope, I headed off to the door.

And died.

Oh, dear.  They *do* do damage.   It's the browns that don't

I hadn't merely not watched the hitpoints.  I'd paid no attention at all
. . .

